  during the preparation and follow-up of  the meeting so that our customers can  have great obedience  one of the lessons i learned very early  on in starting businesses is that first  thing you want to do is when you see a  problem take action rather than wait for  somebody else to solve a problem there's  no reason why you can't take a stab at  solving it yourself and so action is  important but i also learned that really  having a differentiated approach right  what is going to be different about your  product or service what is going to be  different about the way you go to market  and and sell it and  price it right all those things are  really important so it's important to  have do a lot of customer discovery make  sure you really understand the customers  and the problem and have a unique  approach to solving the problem  i think what's interesting about him is  he's this super smart guy but he's also  a little bit different than some  founders because  he didn't really care about having  venture money he didn't really care  about some of the external things but  was focused on  calendly and how to make it work and he  really also just believed in himself in  the way that he threw everything into it  you know he spent down his 401k he flew  into ukraine while it was having its  earlier conflict in order to get uh  software engineers there to develop the  first product he bet everything on this  company  being nigerian means you grew up in a in  an environment in which there's a lot of  economic instability there's also a lot  of political instability and so what  ends up happening is a lot of nigeria's  incredibly resourceful people and when i  look at the success of countless today i  think some of that resourcefulness has  been a huge part of our success  i bootstrapped the company which means i  started the company with my own funds so  capital is very limited in the early  days but i actually attribute this  limited capital to the company's success  today the reason is it forced us to  focus wisely it also focuses to really  understand problems at a deep level  which meant that we could implement  simple effective solutions to solve the  problem  you know i'm really proud of the fact  that last year we crossed 100 million  dollars in revenue that was a huge  milestone for us because if you rewind  back to 10 years ago nobody really knew  that there was a there was a massive  problem to be solved here and the fact  that we've done that has been really  really exciting  [Music]  you
 

